{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1507651-confused-by-lexicon-endowment","id":1507651,"title":"Confused by Lexicon: Endowment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-06T21:25:43-07:00","id":1507651,"title":"Confused by Lexicon: Endowment","content":"What is exactly, in Changeling: the Dreaming 20A, an Endowment? And in which way is it different from a Birthright?<br /> <br /> Or is it just than Kithain have Birthrights and Frailties and the other Fae beings (Thallain, Gallain...) have Endowments and Vulnerabilties?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T07:36:53-07:00","id":1507683,"title":"","content":"A birthright is something you have the right to, an endowment is something you have. So it reads to me like the writer is in character as someone who looks down on the Thallain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T17:24:28-07:00","id":1509651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1507651-confused-by-lexicon-endowment?p=1507683#post1507683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A birthright is something you have the right to, an endowment is something you have. So it reads to me like the writer is in character as someone who looks down on the Thallain.</div> </div> </div> </div>It, somewhat, has to do with free will. A changeling has birthrights because their powers don't define who they are. They aren't slaves. You can see that as Changelings can take both Seelie and Unseelie legacies. Thallain have bestowments, because they exist as slaves (or puppets) of the Fomorians and thus their powers aren't their own. They don't have Free Will, just autonomy (they can never take a seelie legacy).<br /> <br /> Of course, this is thrown out of the window by C20 which gives them Nightmare legacies which, to my knowledge, Changelings <b>cannot take</b>. If they could, then the above argument would stand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}